<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine 5-year T-note rises to 13 pct.</title>
<headline>Philippine 5-year T-note rises to 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield on the Philippine five-year treasury note rose to 13 percent from the previous 12.5 percent, the Bureau of Treasury said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The Bureau was offering notes worth four billion pesos for which it received tenders worth 5.985 billion.</p>
<p>The low was at 12 percent while the average was 12.736 percent.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841 8934</p>
